+
+        // densegemm r1 (EXL3_DENSE_V2 = 1 | 2, EXL3_DENSE_ROWS32 = 1): V2 twin of the tuned kernel,
+        // same grid, bitwise identical; nullptr = not applicable, the served launch below runs.
+        // Entered with any flag on (mode 3 too: the call allocates the workspace the gemv twin uses).
+        // rebase-dev-r2: integer bitrates only (the V2 twins have no half-integer K tables)
+        // rebase165: upstream 3bbc7777 buckets the autotune key by 16 rows up to 64 past 16 rows (and adds
+        // 32/48/64-row tile shapes 5..7). The twins are keyed on the served 16-row-tile config, so they peek
+        // the served bucket (all row counts > 16 -> 16). Tags 1..4 only (shape_compat
